(209003, 11754, 6451, '<td valign="top">Very cute.  I think the photo is a little out of focus though. I really like the comical concept of the photo.  Good job.</td>', 'Very cute.  I think the photo is a little out of focus though. I really like the comical concept of the photo.  Good job.', '2003-02-05 18:49:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(209004, 11829, 6451, '<td valign="top">Very nice image.  The sunrise looks very nice and adds a lot of good lighting for the silhoutee of the person.  Good job.</td>', 'Very nice image.  The sunrise looks very nice and adds a lot of good lighting for the silhoutee of the person.  Good job.', '2003-02-05 18:50:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(209005, 11772, 4815, '<td valign="top">Cats make purr-fect pictures no matter what, I agree. The viewpoint choice is unusual. Creative points for daring to venture into a different perspective. Beautiful golden eyes, whiskers and goatee.  I applaude your effort to capture a family pet in a candid manner as opposed to a stiff planned studio type setup. Informal shots bring out the character and nature of the subject. I take hundreds of shots of our kittens before I get that magical image. If I could suggest a few minor points to consider. Perhaps simplify your background to one tone contrasting with the color of your subject. Eg. play with your cat near a suitable colored blanket. Allow reasonable space around your subject. Enough room so the subject does not look cramped and can visually breathe ( unless you desire to make the opposite popint ). White is hard to expose for, especially with flash as it flares to zero detail easily. A bright side window with sheers or a cotton sheet for diffusing light gives gentle ample lighting with nice natural tones. Keep up the good work.</td>', 'Cats make purr-fect pictures no matter what, I agree. The viewpoint choice is unusual. Creative points for daring to venture into a different perspective. Beautiful golden eyes, whiskers and goatee.  I applaude your effort to capture a family pet in a candid manner as opposed to a stiff planned studio type setup. Informal shots bring out the character and nature of the subject. I take hundreds of shots of our kittens before I get that magical image. If I could suggest a few minor points to consider. Perhaps simplify your background to one tone contrasting with the color of your subject. Eg. play with your cat near a suitable colored blanket. Allow reasonable space around your subject. Enough room so the subject does not look cramped and can visually breathe ( unless you desire to make the opposite popint ). White is hard to expose for, especially with flash as it flares to zero detail easily. A bright side window with sheers or a cotton sheet for diffusing light gives gentle ample lighting with nice natural tones. Keep up the good work.', '2003-02-05 18:51:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(209006, 11977, 6451, '<td valign="top">I really like the organization of this photo.  The colors are very nice and bright as well.  They display a nice image against the background color.  Good job.</td>', 'I really like the organization of this photo.  The colors are very nice and bright as well.  They display a nice image against the background color.  Good job.', '2003-02-05 18:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(209007, 12007, 6561, '<td valign="top">Love this shot!  Meets the challenge, is well balance, good use of black and white, we can almost hear her cry!</td>', 'Love this shot!  Meets the challenge, is well balance, good use of black and white, we can almost hear her cry!', '2003-02-05 18:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
